{"units":[
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:ParseQuantity","summary":"ParseQuantity now calls CacheString on the slow int64 and inf.Dec return paths, so every parsed Quantity carries its canonical string. This is needed because String() no longer caches. It affects every Quantity parsed in the API machinery.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"ParseQuantity now eagerly caches canonical string on result","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Changes the state of every parsed Quantity (the cached s field), which affects equality, serialization cost and DeepEqual.","risk_signals":["public API","hot path for all Quantity parsing","cached string state visible to reflect.DeepEqual"],"focus":["every return path of ParseQuantity sets q.s (fast paths with s: str, zero case, and both new paths)","parse allocation and CPU cost increase for callers that never stringify"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).String","summary":"String() no longer writes the computed string back to the receiver, so it is read-only and race-free. Quantities built without ParseQuantity (NewQuantity, math results) now recompute the string on every call, for example in JSON and proto Size plus Marshal.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"String() stops mutating receiver; no longer caches result","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes the semantics of a widely used public method: caching and mutation behavior, with performance and data-race implications.","risk_signals":["public API","removes receiver mutation","performance on encoding paths","reflect.DeepEqual comparisons relying on cached s"],"focus":["callers that relied on String() populating q.s, such as DeepEqual-based comparisons in tests or semantic equality","encode hot paths for Quantities built via NewQuantity or arithmetic that now recompute the string each call","other code in the package that assumed q.s is set after String()"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).CacheString","summary":"Adds a new public CacheString method that computes the canonical string and stores it on the receiver, for callers that own the instance. It always writes q.s so races are detected more reliably.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add public Quantity.CacheString that stores canonical string","confidence":0.8,"reason":"New public API that mutates the receiver, which can cause data races if called on a shared instance.","risk_signals":["new public API","mutates receiver","concurrency"],"focus":["unconditional write to q.s even when already set, so a call on a shared Quantity races with concurrent readers","nil receiver returns \"<nil>\" consistently with String"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityString","summary":"The test now expects ParseQuantity to set q.s, instead of expecting it to be empty and then filled by String(). The expectation was inverted to match the new behavior, and the check that String() populates q.s was removed.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"test","headline":"TestQuantityString expectations flipped to match eager caching","confidence":0.75,"reason":"Test expectations were changed to match new behavior and an assertion was removed, which could hide a regression.","risk_signals":["assertion removed","expectation changed to match new behavior"],"focus":["that dropping the check that String() sets q.s is intended and covered by TestQuantityCacheString and the Size no-mutation test"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityCacheString","summary":"A new test covers CacheString populating the cached string, idempotence on a second call, and the nil receiver. It is test-only and covers the new method.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add test for Quantity.CacheString behavior","confidence":0.93,"reason":"New test only, with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityString","summary":"The benchmark is rewritten to use sub-benchmarks per quantity and b.Loop, and the Precalc variant is removed because String() no longer caches. It is benchmark-only code.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Rewrite String benchmark with sub-benchmarks and b.Loop","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Benchmark code only, no production behavior.","risk_signals":[]},
